## The Lantern Room

::bg{location="skerry_lantern" time="day"}
@narrator: A hundred and eleven steps, and at the top the great lens, taller than a man, still smelling of paraffin.
@narrator: The clockwork that turns it is jammed with salt and verdigris. A crank handle lies on the floor where it was dropped.
@narrator: On the desk under the window, the keeper's log lies open.
<hub id="lanternLook" prompt="What do you look at?">
  <choice id="clockwork" label="The clockwork" once>
    @narrator: The escapement is seized solid. Someone turned the lens by hand for hours; the brass is polished bright where the palms went.
  </choice>
  <choice id="door" label="The gallery door" once>
    @narrator: The door to the outside gallery has been left on the latch. It bangs gently in the wind.
  </choice>
  <choice id="done" label="Leave the lantern" exit>
    @narrator: You leave the log where it lies. It is not going anywhere.
  </choice>
</hub>
